SUMMARY:Collage on Panel from Start to Finish - September 26th — Sebasto
 pol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
UID:cb474a69161aa175e7d01d4b818bf060@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Collage on Panel from Start to Finish - September 26th\n\n  \n
     \n      \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nS
 aturday\, September 26th\, 2026\; 11 AM - 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials fe
 eAge: 16+ Join French-American collage artist Catherine Cruz for a new com
 prehensive collage workshop designed to guide you through the complete pro
 cess of creating a finished collage on wood panel. Her hands-on process wi
 ll cover every step—from surface preparation and design to varnishing an
 d wiring.  You will learn presentation tips to give your artwork a profes
 sional finish. What you’ll obtain from this workshop:Reliable methods f
 or preparing your panelTechnical information about selected art materialsC
 reative ways to explore abstraction through collageTechniques for presenti
 ng your artIMPORTANT: Each participant must purchase and bring the followi
 ng items:One 12”x12 cradled wood panel\, gallery style 1 ½” thickOne 
 roll of blue painter’s tape 2” wideOne small Phillips screw driver (cr
 oss-shaped)Click Below for MaterialsIMPORTANT: Instructions for where to p
 urchase your materials are provided in the attached PDF.  Each participa
 nt must purchase and bring the items listed in the attached PDF.Materials 
 provided by Instructor: a wide assortment of painted and printed collage p
 apersbrushesacrylic mediumgessovarnishwiring suppliesscissorsThe class wil
 l begin with a demonstration\, so please plan to arrive early to allow tim
 e to settle in.A short lunch break will be held from 12:30 to 1:00 PM. Kin
 dly bring your own lunch and beverage.About the instructor: Catherine Cruz
  is a French-American artist whose work is informed by textures and patter
 ns created by the passing of time and the effects of the natural elements 
 on the built environment.  She holds a Bachelor of Science in interior de
 sign and she worked in the field of architectural design and green buildin
 g certification for over 25 years.  She has taught collage and mixed medi
 a workshops in the Bay Area and in France since 2019\, and this is her fif
 th year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.  Her studio is located in 
 Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Open Studios.  You may cont
 act Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check out Catherine’s other
  classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n        
