DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\nAutumn Gold: Watercolor 
 Basics\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $170.00\n        \n      \
 n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, October 3rd\, 2026 10AM - 4PMCost: $130 + $40 mate
 rials feeCelebrate the richness of autumn with a day of watercolor inspire
 d bySonoma County’s harvest season—pumpkins and winter squash\,persimm
 ons\, seed pods\, turning vines\, all in warm October light. Deepochres\, 
 burnt oranges\, olive greens\, and rich crimson tones inspire loose\,lumin
 ous paintings full of warmth\, texture\, and seasonal abundance.Learn basi
 c watercolor techniques including wet-on-wet painting\, controlledwashes\,
  layering\, color mixing\, and creating texture\, while building strongcom
 positions using color\, light\, and form. Guided discussions explore thees
 sential elements of visual art to help you create expressive\, individualw
 ork.All materials provided. Space limited to 12 students.Discussion break 
 at 12:30 p.m. Please bring a brown bag lunch.About the Instructor: Lynn Za
 chreson studied art at the University of Minnesota and San Jose State Univ
 ersity—Painting\, Printmaking: BA Fine Art. She has experience teaching 
 all ages: Watercolor painting skills\, 30+ years\, Watercolor figure paint
 ing 20+ years\, and Fine Art Basics with Mixed Media 20+ years. Lynn enjoy
 s spending her time painting\, teaching\, long distance hiking\, and garde
 ning. View Lynn’s art here: https://lynnzachresonart.com/\n\n\n\n\n\n   
        \n            Reserve Your Spot
