SUMMARY:SebTown Clay Club: Afterschool Wednesdays  — Sebastopol Center F
 or the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261007T000000
DTEND:20261008T000000
UID:aedb80bfbef13ca5b21d96def5588d7f@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Sale\n      \n\n\n\n\n\nSebTown Clay Club: Wednesday Afterscho
 ol Clay Club (Ages 6-12)\n\n  \n    \n      \n      from $65.00\n    \n  \
 n\nSebTown Clay Club meets on Wednesdays from 1:00-4:30pm.Students May Arr
 ive Late. Join us on Wednesday’s for a special Youth Clay Club\,  focuse
 d on fostering space for ceramics creative freedoms while exploring clay b
 uilding techniques to make themed creations each week. Every three weeks\,
  we have a new theme that allows students to explore their imaginations an
 d create what they want to see. In Sebastopol\, students are out of school
  early on Wednesdays\, as early as 1:00pm. Instead of focusing on a projec
 t driven\, or specific skill\, we are offering a ceramics series in which 
 students are encouraged to create what they would like with the supervisio
 n and guidance of an instructor to facilitate the learning needs of the st
 udent. Students will be given an outside play break from 2:45-3:15 where t
 hey can enjoy snacks and group games. This can be purchased as a 9 session
  bundle\, 3-session series\, or drop-in (single day) registrations.3-Sessi
 on Series: $105 + $25 Clay Fee9 Sessions: $315 + $75 Clay Fee (Currently o
 n sale for early bird registrations $30 off!) Drop-In Same-Day Sessions: $
 40 + $25 Clay Fee SebTown Clay Club SessionsCreepy Cryptids\, Monsters\, a
 nd Ghouls: October 7th\, October 14th\, October 21stUnder the Fantasea: Go
 ing Underwater : October 28th\, November 4th\, November 18thCerama-Mini Ma
 nia: Faeries\, Goblins\, and Elves - Oh My! December 2nd\, December 9th\, 
 December 16thAbout the Instructor: Rogelio Cruz is our Youth Arts Coordina
 tor who will be facilitating and teaching this program. Rogelio Cruz is a 
 visual and performing artist born and raised in Sonoma County. They gradua
 ted from San Francisco State University with a BA in Fine Arts and a minor
  in dance. Rogelio is driven by a dedication to furthering the accessibili
 ty of art and arts\, and their teaching philosophy is centered around faci
 litating a space for all to freely learn and grow in their creative proces
 s. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  Sessions:\n                \n\n\n\n 
                      Select Sessions\n                    \nCreepy Cryptid
 s\, Monsters\, and Ghouls: October 7th\, October 14th\, October 21st\nUnde
 r the Fantasea: Going Underwater : October 28th\, November 4th\, November 
 18th\nCerama-Mini Mania: Faeries\, Goblins\, and Elves - Oh My! December 2
 nd\, December 9th\, December 16th\nAll 9 Sessions\nOne-Time Drop-In (same 
 day)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
