BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Drawing Portraits From Photos (3 Session Class) 
 — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261104T000000
DTEND:20261105T000000
UID:5f6df1c0b287b389a6476337ca7978d0@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Introduction to Drawing Portraits From Photos (3 Session Class
 )\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $165.00\n        \n      \n    
 \n  \n\nIntroduction to Drawing Portraits from Photos November 4th\, 11th
 \, and 18th 6:00-9:00pm $150.00 + $15.00 Materials Fee = $165.00 Age Re
 stricted to 18+ About this class: In this three week course\, students w
 ill learn and practice observational skills and fundamental drawing techni
 ques while learning the basics of drawing portraits from photographs. Dra
 wing human faces requires the same basic drawing skills that one employs f
 or any subject - observing proportion\, flattening shapes\, and utilizing 
 line or value to convey volume. But the conceptual weight of human faces t
 ends to intimidate artists. When drawing any subject\, the hardest skill i
 s simply learning to see\, a skill that anyone can be taught\, practice\, 
 and hone. This course will focus on the practice of looking\, and discover
 ing strategies to find objectivity when rendering portraits. This class i
 s for anyone who wants to practice and advance their drawing skills - begi
 nners\, those who haven’t practiced in years\, or any artists who just w
 ant to learn new techniques and practice their skills with consistent feed
 back and guidance. Through demonstration\, practice\, and reflective discu
 ssion\, this class will explore the foundations of rendering human express
 ion with classical drawing techniques in a low pressure environment. Obse
 rvational drawing gives all artists a foundation of practical knowledge an
 d skills that infinitely expands the possibilities of what one can create.
  If your ideas feel limited by your drawing skills\, if you feel frustrate
 d or stuck in your painting practice\, or if you simply want to start draw
 ing and are looking for a place to start\, this is the class for you.About
  the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Arts with an emphasi
 s on drawing and printmaking from University of San Diego\, then attended 
 University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in printmaking. Hannah’
 s etchings have been internationally shown and collected\, but her art pra
 ctice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, and watercolor. She has tau
 ght all ages in many mediums. These days\, Hannah primarily teaches waterc
 olor\, observational drawing\, and paper cutting. You can view her work at
  www.hannahdrawstrees.com \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n             
    Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/introduction-to-drawing-portr
 aits-from-photos-3-session-class
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
