BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Winter Botanicals: 2 Session Watercolor Workshop — Sebastopol Ce
 nter For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261108T000000
DTEND:20261109T000000
UID:0bb1bd30a57ec5b5ac59cf3856c65f81@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Winter Botanicals: Watercolor Workshop\n\n  \n    \n      \n  
       \n          $125.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nWinter Botanicals
 : Watercolor Workshop (2 Sessions) November 8th and November 15th\, 2026
  1:00-4:00pm $110.00 + $15.00 Materials Fee = $125.00 Age restricted to
  18+About this class: In this two week workshop\, students will learn a u
 nique approach to watercolor\, intended to address the frustration that ma
 ny feel with this challenging medium. The class will focus on strengthenin
 g one’s observational skills\, while learning a watercolor technique tha
 t teaches the artist to see value and color. Over the two weeks we will w
 ork on 1 painting\, progressing through guided steps to build a luminous b
 otanical painting. With a mix of demonstrations and individualized instruc
 tion\, students of all experience levels will develop new skills and have 
 a meaningful creative experience. Our subject will be seasonal botanicals
 \, the iconic and recognizable plants that decorate our holiday season\, s
 uch as holly and poinsettias. These subjects are great for beginners and m
 aster painters alike\; their organic shapes are forgiving drawing subjects
 \, but their beauty can be a muse for life. Instructor Hannah Day is a pa
 ssionate plant painter and will share her unique approach to rendering bot
 anicals. This class will work from photos\, practicing observational drawi
 ng\, in addition to watercolor technique. Beginning artists and repeat st
 udents are welcome.About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Vis
 ual Arts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from University of Sa
 n Diego\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA i
 n printmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally shown and col
 lected\, but her art practice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, and
  watercolor. She has taught all ages in many mediums. These days\, Hannah 
 primarily teaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, and paper cutting. 
 You can view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n     
          \n                Add to cart
